WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.639
Speaker 1: All right, welcome to the show.

00:00:01.639 --> 00:00:06.270
It's my last day in the bunker for a little
bit and there is much to discuss.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:11.080
And you know, this first story I'm going to
talk about, there's sort of some risk to even

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:19.699
talking about this story because the issue
of Donald Trump and Russia has become so weaponized

00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:26.650
and so distorted and so partizan and toxic
and tribal, it's become so disconnected from

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:33.320
the actual facts that we know that there is
a risk to even bringing this issue up again.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.910
But there is news that continues to fill out
the story and our understanding of what took

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.400
place before and during the Trump administration.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.870
And we learned some important things over
the weekend about coordination between the

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.870
Trump 2016 campaign and Russian intelligence.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:55.400
And since we've covered the story all along,
it would be weird if I didn't tell you that

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:02.360
there is new information and there are some
in my audience I know who referred to the

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:08.549
story as Russia Gate and referred to me as
a Russia greater conspiracy hoax.

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:12.189
Whatever, whatever the terms now are on the
story.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:18.340
But my my core audience, who has been with
us, you know, at least back to 2017, knows

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:25.120
that my position on Trump Russia was there
will be no personal collusion found between

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.149
Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin at a personal
level.

00:01:28.149 --> 00:01:33.280
There's not going to be any smoking gun video
of Trump and Putin planning anything with

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.889
regard to Donald Trump's candidacy.

00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:40.280
But it looks like a duck and it sounds like
a duck and it walks like a duck.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.579
Something approximating a duck is probably
there.

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:47.399
And indeed, we had more than a dozen indictments
in the Mueller probe.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:52.920
There was communication and coordination between
Trump and Russia, including through WikiLeaks

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.689
as an intermediary.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:02:00.320
Paul Manafort in touch with Russians regarding
polling and the campaign and on and on.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.340
It was never going to remove Donald Trump.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.659
Go back to my videos from April of 2017, where
I made it clear Trump was never going to be

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:11.569
charged or end up in prison as a result of
whatever it was he did or didn't do with Vladimir

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:12.569
Putin.

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:16.950
Because I don't I don't want to say no one
believed, but our show was not saying they

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.049
will be caught having done anything.

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:24.550
But it was likely all along a combination
of Trump being sort of a useful idiot, not

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:31.689
even realizing how his mere candidacy, his
mere presidency, helps Russia's goal of destabilizing

00:02:31.689 --> 00:02:34.489
Western democracies for their gain.

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:39.830
And some of the people around Trump were actually
in touch with Russians and coordinating.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:46.780
So, OK, there's a new report, and this is
a Treasury Department deport report, which

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:54.040
now quietly in twenty, twenty one years after
the entire fiasco with Trump already gone,

00:02:54.040 --> 00:03:02.269
confirms that Donald Trump's 2016 campaign
was sharing information with a Russian intelligence

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:03.269
officer.

00:03:03.269 --> 00:03:04.269
Full stop.

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:06.879
That's the story during the 2016 election.

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:11.189
Russian and Ukrainian political consultant
Konstantin Kilim Nick, we've mentioned this

00:03:11.189 --> 00:03:18.930
name before, was providing Russia with so-called
sensitive information on polling and Trump

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.290
campaign strategy.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:27.989
KMB Nick, quote, sought to promote the narrative
that Ukraine, not Russia, had interfered in

00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:31.239
the 2016 US presidential election in 2018.

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:32.310
Kill him.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:37.769
Nick was indicted on obstruction of justice
charges for his unregistered lobbying work

00:03:37.769 --> 00:03:39.930
related to Ukraine.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:46.810
But this same Treasury report now spells out
that KMB Nick had been coordinating with Donald

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.959
Trump's campaign chairman, Paul Manafort,
during the 2016 election.

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:55.780
The Treasury report refers to kill him as
a Russian intelligence officer.

00:03:55.780 --> 00:04:02.120
Donald Trump's campaign manager, church campaign
chairman for a period of time, was coordinating

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:07.099
with a man now regarded as a described as
a Russian intelligence officer.

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:13.120
And Manafort repeatedly shared internal campaign
information with KMB Nick.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.940
As Mother Jones writes, Manafort passed inside
info from the Trump campaign to kill him.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:19.940
Nick kill him.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.860
Nick gave it to Russian intelligence, which
at the time was mounting a covert attack on

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:30.380
the 2016 election to thwart Hillary Clinton
and help Donald Trump.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:31.380
That's collusion.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.810
Now, it isn't the cartoonish scenarios that
some dreamed up Trump secretly meeting with

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:43.700
Putin personally, but it is Trump's campaign
chairman scheming with a Russian intelligence

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:47.950
officer as Russia was publishing derogatory
information about Trump's opponent, Hillary

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.670
Clinton, and preferred Trump over Hillary.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.520
We don't have to get all dramatic.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.130
We don't have to get hyperbolic.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.389
They were working together.

00:04:56.389 --> 00:04:57.590
That's it.

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:58.790
It's simple.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:04.139
Meanwhile, at the same time, kill him, Nic
was trying to use Paul Manafort and through

00:05:04.139 --> 00:05:09.530
him use Trump to advance Vladimir Putin's
interests related to Ukraine.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.060
This isn't unique.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.710
Many countries try to do this.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:17.400
Many of them just aren't as good as Russia
at doing it.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:23.390
And many countries don't have someone as vulnerable
and naive and ignorant as Donald Trump and

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:25.030
the people that Donald Trump put around him.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:26.820
And it really went both ways.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:32.930
So for those who will react to this with like
an OK, so what type of approach?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.509
Imagine for a moment that it was revealed
today, for example.

00:05:36.509 --> 00:05:37.900
It just hasn't happened.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:43.830
But imagine imagine we learned today Joe Biden's
campaign manager was in regular contact with

